Export the wasm-c-api (`wasm_*`) symbols from the shared library on GCC/Clang.

The top-level CMakeLists.txt compiles with `-fvisibility=hidden`, and
`WASM_API_EXTERN` is empty outside of MSVC, so none of the wasm-c-api functions
(`wasm_engine_new`, `wasm_module_new`, ...) end up in the dynamic symbol table of
libiwasm.so/.dylib; only `wasm_runtime_*` is exported (via `WASM_RUNTIME_API_EXTERN`).

This should be sent upstream (no upstream issue/PR exists yet).

diff --git a/core/iwasm/include/wasm_c_api.h b/core/iwasm/include/wasm_c_api.h
index 241a0ee..00920ad 100644
--- a/core/iwasm/include/wasm_c_api.h
+++ b/core/iwasm/include/wasm_c_api.h
@@ -22,6 +22,8 @@
 #else
 #define WASM_API_EXTERN __declspec(dllimport)
 #endif
+#elif defined(__GNUC__) || defined(__clang__)
+#define WASM_API_EXTERN __attribute__((visibility("default")))
 #else
 #define WASM_API_EXTERN
 #endif
